<% seo title: "About · Tastatur",
       description: "Why Tastatur exists: a portfolio of side projects worth measuring, and no " \
                    "wish to use tracking cookies to do it. Built by Reedster LLC, AGPL-3.0.",
       structured_data: :about %>
<% maintainer = Tastatur.maintainer %>

<div class="shell">
  <div class="pt-5 rule-heavy mb-12 max-w-3xl">
    <p class="label mt-5 mb-3">About</p>
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-semibold tracking-[-0.03em]">Why this exists</h1>
  </div>

  <div class="lg:grid lg:grid-cols-12 gap-10">
    <div class="lg:col-span-7">
      <%# The origin story, in the words of the person who had the problem.
          Kept first-person and kept short: it is the most credible thing on the
          site precisely because it is not a value proposition. -%>
      <blockquote class="text-[19px] leading-relaxed border-l-2 border-signal pl-6 mb-10">
        <p class="mb-4">
          I have a portfolio of projects that I want to see what people do on them, but I do not
          like using tracking cookies to do this, so a lot of services were cut out.
        </p>
        <p>
          I enjoy building projects, and worked on this to monitor all of my projects.
        </p>
        <footer class="label mt-6 not-italic">
          Sean Reed<span class="mx-2">·</span><%= maintainer[:name] %>
        </footer>
      </blockquote>

      <div class="space-y-5 text-[15px] text-ink-2 leading-relaxed max-w-2xl">
        <p>
          That is the whole brief. Nothing about Tastatur is designed to win a feature comparison
          against the large analytics platforms, because the reason for building it was that those
          platforms already ruled themselves out.
        </p>
        <p>
          It also explains the shape of the thing. A tool built for someone with a handful of side
          projects has to install in one line, run on a small box, and never need attention. It has
          no reason to add a data-warehouse integration or an audience-segmentation builder, and it
          has every reason to be honest about what cookieless measurement genuinely cannot do,
          because the person reading those caveats is the person who wrote them.
        </p>
        <p>
          Tastatur is free software under the AGPL-3.0. Run it yourself, read every line, or use the
          hosted version and let someone else keep it patched. The
          <%= link_to "source is public", maintainer[:source], class: "underline hover:text-signal", rel: "noopener" %>,
          which is the only reason any of the privacy claims on this site are worth more than a
          promise.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-3 mt-9">
        <%= link_to "What it collects", privacy_path, class: "btn" %>
        <%= link_to "How to use it", docs_path, class: "btn btn-quiet" %>
      </div>
    </div>

    <%# --- Who builds it -%>
    <div class="mt-10 lg:mt-0 lg:col-span-5 lg:border-l lg:border-rule lg:pl-10">
      <p class="label mb-4">Built and maintained by</p>

      <div class="card">
        <div class="card-body">
          <p class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-[-0.02em]"><%= maintainer[:name] %></p>
          <p class="text-[13px] text-ink-2 mt-1.5"><%= maintainer[:tagline] %></p>
          <p class="text-[13px] text-ink-2 mt-4 leading-relaxed">
            A solo software practice run by Sean Reed, working mostly in Ruby on Rails and on AI
            engineering. Tastatur is developed and supported there.
          </p>
          <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2 mt-5">
            <%= link_to "reedster.llc", maintainer[:url], class: "btn btn-sm", rel: "noopener" %>
            <%= link_to "Source", maintainer[:source], class: "btn btn-quiet btn-sm", rel: "noopener" %>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="card-body border-t border-rule bg-surface-2">
          <p class="label mb-3">This instance</p>
          <% if Tastatur.legal_configured? %>
            <p class="text-[13px]">
              Operated by <strong><%= Tastatur.legal_value(:entity) %></strong>.
              <%= link_to "Privacy policy", privacy_policy_path, class: "underline hover:text-signal" %>
              and <%= link_to "terms", terms_path, class: "underline hover:text-signal" %>.
            </p>
          <% else %>
            <p class="text-[13px] text-ink-2">
              <% if Tastatur.self_hosted? %>
                A self-hosted install. Whoever runs it is the data controller, not
                <%= maintainer[:name] %>.
              <% else %>
                The operator of this instance has not been configured yet.
              <% end %>
            </p>
          <% end %>
        </div>
      </div>

      <%# Authorship and operator are different facts, and a self-hoster reading
          this page needs to know which one applies to them. -%>
      <p class="text-[12px] text-muted mt-4 leading-relaxed">
        <%= maintainer[:name] %> wrote the software. That is true of every copy of it. Who is
        responsible for the data in <em>this</em> instance depends on who is running it, which is
        why the two are stated separately.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
